  "id": "DrugBank_DB01030 - MONDO_16249",
  "verbalization": "Topotecan, through its indication for Ovarian Adenocarcinoma, Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor of Ovary, and Ovarian Mucinous Adenocarcinoma, is linked to Cisplatin, which in turn is associated with Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. This suggests a potential pathway where Topotecan may influence the development of ovarian cancers, which are treated with Cisplatin, and thus indirectly contribute to the development of Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a possible role of Topotecan in the pathogenesis of ovarian cancer, which is a known precursor to Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. The mechanism appears to involve the use of Cisplatin in the treatment of ovarian cancers, which may have a role in the development of the syndrome, though the exact relationship remains to be clarified.",
